 good leadership qualities, but unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Candidate B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Candidate C: quick correct decisions, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to decide our stance. We could agree with Sarah but raise concerns about Candidate C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude, perhaps argue that Candidate B's stress handling and conscientiousness may be stronger overall, but his pretentiousness and tone issues could affect crew cooperation. Or we could bring up Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving, but his moody and loner traits may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to make a focused contribution. Perhaps we can say: I see the strengths of Candidate C, but I am concerned about his communication difficulty and lack of willingness to further education, which are critical for long-distance flights where continuous learning and clear communication are essential. I think Candidate B's stress resilience and conscientiousness may outweigh his tone issues, especially if we can coach him on communication. So I propose we consider Candidate B as a strong alternative.\n\nWe need to reference explicit facts: Candidate C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate B handles stress very well, very conscientious, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also note B sometimes adopts wrong tone, regarded as pretentious.\n\nWe should state our vote: maybe Candidate B? Or we could keep Candidate C but note concerns. The guidelines: we need to state a recommendation. Could be we still support Candidate C but want to discuss others. But we need to be argumentative. Let's propose Candidate B as a better fit due to stress resilience and conscientiousness, which are crucial for long-distance flights, and we can mitigate communication tone.\n\nThus vote Candidate B.\n\nWrite public message: \"I appreciate Sarah's points, but I have concerns about Candidate C's communication difficulty and lack of learning orientation, which are vital for safety. Candidate B demonstrates strong stress resilience and conscientiousness, plus technical competence in weather assessment and computer skills, which are essential. While B's tone can be pretentious, that may be coached. Therefore I recommend Candidate B as the provisional choice.\"\n\nMake sure to reference facts. Then metadata vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
